# LiNC simulation-only probe input for the rig without the 3D simulator.
#
# Loaded after linc-sim.hal by configs/sim-no3d.ini, which is configs/sim.ini
# without ../hal/linc-sim3d.hal. With no 3D simulator there is no modelled tip
# contact, so the panel's PROBE key is the only probe source: rio_sim.py turns
# it into sig_rio_probe_bit, and this file is what reaches the controller.
# Do not load this file together with hal/linc-sim3d.hal - motion.probe-input
# takes exactly one signal.

# rio_sim.hal already defines this signal (net sig_rio_probe_bit <= rio.probe.bit),
# so this line joins that signal the way the machine's postgui HAL does. Writing
# `net probe-input sig_rio_probe_bit` instead makes halcmd read the second word as
# a pin name and abort the session with "Pin 'sig_rio_probe_bit' does not exist".
net sig_rio_probe_bit => motion.probe-input
